    fxDeepReadyN: "Deep X-ray ready: {n} sourced fact(s).", fxDeepCached: "Deep X-ray already existed (less than 7 days old). Use re-run to redo it.", fxDeepNoSite: "This lead has no site: there is nothing to research.", fxDeepNoFacts: "The research ran but no fact had a valid source. No invented dossier was saved.", fxDeepFail: "Could not research right now.", fxDeepConfirmDel: "Delete the deep X-ray for this lead? You can run it again later.", fxDeepDeleted: "Deep X-ray deleted.", fxDeepDelFail: "Could not delete.",
    autXEyebrow: "Automation · Research", autXTitle: "Automatic deep X-ray", autXToggleTip: "Researches whoever replies, on its own. Cold leads never enter.", autXStatusOn: "ON (researches whoever replies)", autXStatusOff: "off (only via the button on the lead card)", autXDesc: "Opens the lead's site with a real browser, reads the text of the pages (not just the meta tags), follows the public bio of the socials the site links to and searches for recent news. Then it distils a dossier where every fact carries the link of the page it was read on: the server drops any fact whose source was not actually read, so the agent cannot invent. You can audit everything on the lead card, and delete and redo it.", autXDailyCap: "Daily research cap", autXCapNote: "About 0.02 USD per lead. Beyond this cap, the AI Agent's hourly, daily and monthly cost limits apply. The result is cached for 7 days (re-running the same lead does not spend again).", autXConfirmOn: "Turn on the automatic deep X-ray?\n\nWhen a lead REPLIES, the system opens their site with a real browser, reads up to 6 pages, follows the socials and searches for news, then writes a dossier where every fact carries the link it came from. The agent reads that before replying.\n\nIt costs about 2 cents per lead and takes half a minute. Cold leads NEVER enter (only those who reply). There is a daily cap and the usual cost limits.\n\nContinue?",
    autDEyebrow: "Automation · Diagnosis", autDTitle: "Auto-diagnosis", autDToggleTip: "Turn the auto-diagnosis on or off", autDDesc: "diagnoses leads without an analysis on its own and feeds the smart reply.", autDDailyCap: "Diagnoses per day cap", autDCapNote: "Just a cost brake: each analysis spends AI calls. It runs on the server, without touching your sending reputation (analysing is not sending). The full diagnosis (deep site and Google) needs the worker and Places configured; without them it does the analysis it can and the lead card marks \"partial analysis\".", autDConfirmOn: "Turn on the auto-diagnosis? The system will diagnose leads without an analysis by itself (site and Google), on the server, at any time. Analysing does not touch your sending reputation, it only spends AI cost, so the only limit is the daily cap below. The diagnosis lands on the lead's card and the smart reply reads it before writing. Continue?",
    autSaved: "Automation updated.", autSaveFail: "The server did not confirm; nothing changed.", autNetFail: "No server connection; nothing changed.",
    autREyebrow: "Automation · Replies", autRTitle: "Smart replies", autRDesc: "When a lead replies off-script, the system reads their history and the atelier's persona, then writes a reply in ABiL's voice, in their language. Choose how far to automate:", autRStatusSuggest: "· SUGGESTION (you approve sending)", autRStatusAuto: "· AUTONOMOUS (locked: suggests only)", autRStatusOff: "· off", autRHardOff: "Under construction: even in autonomous mode, ABiL only SUGGESTS the reply, it never sends on its own while the site is not live.", autRGmailNote: "Needs Gmail connected (in Connections) so the system can read the leads' replies.", autRSuggestLabel: "Autonomous suggestion", autRSuggestTip: "Generates the reply on its own, but does not send", autRSuggestDesc: "Generates the smart reply automatically when the lead replies, but does not send it. The suggestion stays on the lead's card for you to approve sending, one by one.", autRAutoLabel: "Autonomous reply", autRAutoTip: "Generates and sends to the lead on its own (locked in teaser)", autRAutoDesc: "Generates and sends the reply to the lead on its own, without approval. Leave off until you trust the system. Safeguard: it escalates to you when it detects a purchase, price or contract.", autRPromptLabel: "How the system should reply (instruction)", autRConfirmAuto: "Turn on AUTONOMOUS REPLY? The system would reply to leads on its own, in your voice, without waiting for approval. Note: while the site is under construction, a server safeguard blocks sending, so it will only SUGGEST the drafts. Continue?",
